{"ld": 246, "paper": "SP112", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Establish the Option of Sentencing Alternatives for Primary Caregivers", "sponsor_id": "s-talbot-ross-rachel", "cosponsor_ids": ["s-beebe-center-anne", "s-carney-anne", "h-hasenfus-tavis", "s-hickman-craig", "h-kuhn-amy", "h-lee-adam", "h-sato-eleanor"], "committee_code": "JUD", "committee_name": "Judiciary", "summary": {"text": "This bill requires a court in sentencing a defendant convicted of an offense that may result in a term of imprisonment, upon motion of the defendant and supported by an affidavit, to consider a sentencing alternative other than imprisonment due to the defendant's being a primary caregiver of a minor, elderly dependent or individual with a physical or mental disability. In making the decision, the court is required to consider factors such as the nature and circumstances of the offense, the history and character of the defendant, the defendant's family circumstances and relationships and the impact of any sentence considered on every individual for whom the defendant is the primary caregiver. The court is required to make written findings of the court's decision before issuing the sentence.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0112&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Enacted", "final_disposition": {"label": "Enacted", "date": "2025-06-22", "governor_action": "Unsigned", "governor_action_date": "2025-06-22"}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 246)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0112&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (S-253)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0112&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}, {"label": "Amendment C-B (S-254)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0112&item=3&snum=132", "item": 3}], "amendments": [{"id": 